<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69554" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μώϊον</span></b> , τό, Egyptian
		word for a <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>receptacle, box</i>
			or <i>jar,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PHib.
				1.49.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PPetr.</u>
				3p.186
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκωμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PSI</u>
					4.428.78
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>; prob. also a measure of capacity, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀχύρου μώϊα μα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ostr.Bodl.</u>
					i231
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span>: pl. written 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μώεια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
					167.7
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>; sg. written 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μούειον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					146.3
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(vi A. D.)</span>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μώστιον</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
